{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"852766832552837160","content":"( <@!260820438026813440> - since this is your area, I feel like I need to ping you specifically here; I intend to apply this to the other games as well, with your approval, but this is naturally the one I'm gravitating to because Let Kukudh Play Ring Toss™️\nI will accept if this takes more pigment than it normally would (I have 200 essence worth), I will also accept if the making of some non-metal weapons in the process doesn't work out - all I know for certain is that I want 2 shortbows because I know two people who want them.\nthis isn't Sabrine's idea - my current thoughts are either patron or fae compulsion (hence the eyes), but obviously up to you (third option, some memory of childhood))\n\n\nSabrine, eyes void, takes out an odd, shimmering palette of paint - marvellous pigments. As if in a trance, she begins to paint over the ruins.\nShe paints the ring toss stall, just as it was before. She paints a few weapons on its counter: a couple of shortbows, some boomerangs, a quarterstaff or two. And instead of the magical prizes - something tells her she can't replicate those... - she taps into memories of a childhood she never new, and paints plush toys - of Grimlock, of the Mender, of other symbols of Empire City, intending to bring back hope to the remaining people.","created_at":"2021-07-16T12:56:13.443000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-16T13:00:47.520000Z","id":"865577566231855154","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
